title: Blow the Man Down
artist: Traditional
origin: England
culture: English
genre: Sea shanty
language: en
key: C major
tempo: 176
meter: 6/8
pickup: 1
intro: 2
outro: 1
style: shanty
guide: ooh
year: 1867
attribution: Anonymous halyard shanty of the Atlantic packet ships, quoted in print by 1867 and published in L. A. Smith's The Music of the Waters (1888); the words here are stanzas 1 and 4 of R. R. Terry's The Shanty Book (1921). Traditional melody and words, public domain worldwide.
source_url: https://abcnotation.com/tunePage?a=sniff.numachi.com/~rickheit/dtrad/abc_dtrad.tar.gz/abc_dtrad/BLOWDOWN/0000
tags: sea shanty, sailor, singalong, waltz time, work song
# Written in 6/8 with the eighth note as the beat (6 beats per bar); a dotted quarter is (3).
# Two stanzas, 8 bars each, each starting with a one-eighth pickup. Source is in D; transposed to C.

chords:
| C | C | C F | Dm G7 | G7 | Dm | G7 | C |
| C | C | C F | Dm G7 | G7 | Dm | G7 | C |

melody:
Oh, blow the man down, bul-lies, blow the man down,
E4 G4 A4 G4 E4 C4 E4 G4 A4 G4 E4(2)
to me way-ay, blow the man down!
C4/ E4/ G4(3) A4(3) F4. E4/ F4 D4(2)
Oh, blow the man down, bul-lies, blow him a-way,
E4 F4 G4 F4 D4 B3 D4 F4 E4 D4 A4(3)
give me some time to blow the man down!
G4 G4 G4 G4(2) F4 E4. D4/ E4 C4(2)

As I was a-walk-ing down Win-ches-ter Street,
E4 G4 A4 G4 E4 C4 E4 G4 A4 G4 E4(2)
to me way-ay, blow the man down!
C4/ E4/ G4(3) A4(3) F4. E4/ F4 D4(2)
a sau-cy young dam-sel I hap-pened to meet,
E4 F4 G4 F4 D4 B3 D4 F4 E4 D4 A4(3)
give me some time to blow the man down!
G4 G4 G4 G4(2) F4 E4. D4/ E4 C4(3)
